title: 'statement-store: reject statements without topics'
doc:
- audience: Node Dev
  description: |-
    The statement store rejects a statement without topics on submit from every source: the
    network, an RPC client and the runtime. The result is `SubmitResult::Invalid` with the new
    `InvalidReason::NoTopics`, which has the metrics label `no_topics` and the RPC reason
    `noTopics`. Such a statement was treated as a broadcast and went to every peer whatever
    filter the peer advertised.

    The affinity filter matches a statement only by its topics. A database migration to version 4
    drops the statements without topics that a store already holds. The migration is one way: an
    older binary refuses to open the migrated database.
- audience: Node Operator
  description: |-
    The statement store migrates its database to version 4 at the first startup and drops the
    stored statements without topics. A node that has started with this change refuses to start
    on an older binary until its statement database is removed.
crates:
- name: sp-statement-store
  bump: major
- name: sc-statement-store
  bump: patch
- name: sc-network-statement
  bump: patch
- name: sc-rpc-api
  bump: patch
- name: sc-rpc-spec-v2
  bump: patch
